 "notes": "The 10-K gives only workforce demographics and points to the separate Corporate Responsibility Report, so this rescore relies mainly on the report. Several figures are small in absolute terms because Host has only about 163 employees. WIN is open to all employees and is women-focused. The 3 rests on the rubric's explicit example (an employee network with membership figures) plus multiple other activities with figures; a stricter reading of 'several small activities' could argue for 2. Items excluded or not counted: the Sunflower Bakery partnership at Gaithersburg is described as a pilot and was not cited. The Dreyfus BOLD/GRACE investment was excluded because the donations are made by Dreyfus, not Host, and the social impact funds also cover non-inclusion aims. Hotel-manager inclusion 'best practices' (recruiting veterans and refugees) are general and not specific to Host. The 2030 supplier and inclusion targets are planned. The pay equity study was a past activity. ADA accessibility is legal compliance and was not scored."}
